  "term": "colony",
  "definition": "In this historical source, colony can mean a group shaped by locality in social usage, a biologically organized group of relatively distinct living units, or in political philosophy a community of emigrants settled away from their mother country and still under its protection or government. It can also refer to such settlers as a distinct self-governing community.",
